# Tailwind CSS v4

## Setup (this repo)

- Entry: `src/app/globals.css` with `@import "tailwindcss";`
- Tokens via `@theme inline` mapping to CSS variables
- PostCSS plugin: `@tailwindcss/postcss` in `postcss.config.mjs`
- **No** `tailwind.config.js` unless a plugin absolutely requires it — prefer CSS-first config

## Token rules

Define brand colors, fonts, and radii as CSS variables in `:root`, then expose them in `@theme inline`:

```css
:root {
  --background: #09090b;
  --accent: #3b82f6;
}

@theme inline {
  --color-background: var(--background);
  --color-accent: var(--accent);
  --font-sans: var(--font-geist-sans);
}
```

- Prefer semantic utilities: `bg-background`, `text-accent`, `border-white/10`.
- Do not hard-code one-off hex values in JSX when a token exists — extend tokens instead.
- Keep the dark charcoal + electric blue system; do not introduce purple/indigo default AI themes.

## Utility guidance

- Use responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) mobile-first.
- Prefer spacing/typography scale consistency (`gap-4`, `p-6`, `text-sm` / `text-base` / `text-4xl`).
- Glass cards: `border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] backdrop-blur-sm` (or existing equivalents).
- Avoid `@apply` except rare shared primitives; compose utilities in JSX.
- Avoid large arbitrary-value sprawl (`w-[137px]`) — use scale or a token.

## Performance

- Rely on Tailwind’s generated CSS; do not duplicate large custom CSS for the same effect.
- Keep decorative gradients/grids in CSS classes (e.g. `.grid-glow`), not inline style objects, when reusable.
